 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>A <b>simple servlet</b> is a class that extends <b>HttpServlet</b> and overrides <b>doGet()</b> or <b>doPost()</b> to send an HTML response.</p><h3>Steps</h3><ul><li>Create a class that <b>extends HttpServlet</b>.</li><li>Override <b>doGet(HttpServletRequest, HttpServletResponse)</b>.</li><li>Set content type: <code>res.setContentType(\"text/html\")</code>.</li><li>Get writer: <code>PrintWriter out = res.getWriter()</code>.</li><li>Write HTML with <code>out.println()</code>.</li><li>Map URL with <code>@WebServlet(\"/hello\")</code> or web.xml, deploy on Tomcat.</li></ul>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which method gives the PrintWriter?",
  "options": [
   "req.getWriter()",
   "res.getWriter()",
   "out.getWriter()"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Every Dog Takes Walks: W = Writer from response."
 }
